# Omni colour tokens

All colours are defined once in `src/app/globals.css`. Never hardcode a hex or
`rgba()` colour in a component.

| Purpose | Tokens |
| --- | --- |
| Surfaces (back to front) | `sunken` `canvas` `surface` `raised` `elevated` |
| Text | `ink` `ink-soft` `ink-faint` `ink-invert` |
| Brand: primary actions, solid reporting lines, filled seats | `brand` `brand-hi` `brand-soft` |
| Signal: secondary/dotted-line relationships, planning mode | `signal` `signal-hi` `signal-soft` |
| Semantic | `positive` `caution` (vacancies) `critical` |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<div className="bg-[#22d3ee] text-[#071018] shadow-[0_8px_20px_rgba(34,211,238,0.2)]" />

// ✅ GOOD
<div className="bg-brand text-ink-invert shadow-[0_8px_20px_rgba(0,0,0,0.35)]" />
```

Use `/NN` for opacity (`bg-raised/70`, `border-caution/45`). For inline styles
and SVG (React Flow edges), use `var(--color-brand)`.

Shadows are neutral black. Only tint a shadow with brand when it signals state
(selection, focus, active) — never for decoration.

## Two rules that are easy to get wrong

**Colour-bearing CSS must be layered.** An unlayered rule outranks
`@layer utilities`, so an unlayered `* { border-color: ... }` silently kills
every `border-<colour>` utility. Keep such defaults inside `@layer base`.

**Two places may still use literal hex:**
- `src/app/global-error.tsx` — renders its own document without `globals.css`.
- Department/group colours — user data persisted to the database, not theme.
